      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BREWERY LANE (1) has been a bit hot and cold and that continued last start when he finished third, beaten 8 metres, in a better performance at Narrogin over 2662m. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Tackles a similar assignment and he can get up without surprising. EYE BETTER (9) was out of the money two back at Gloucester Park. Turned in a better run last time out when second over 2190m at this track, beaten 2.5 metres. Draws out a little on the second line and may need luck at some point. This should be an easier assignment so she is in the right race to find winning form. VINTAGE BLU (3) disappointed last time when tenth over 2185m at Pinjarra. Can bounce back. RIPPER VIEW (2) should be at her peak at the fourth run back from a spell, the latest outing a fourth at Narrogin a week ago.",
